From 7588529955a1e64afeabff26abce5d64bcbd64f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marc infield <marc@infield.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:21:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(machines): Sienci AltMill 2x4, 4x4 and 4x8 on the
 grblHAL post

Three built-in machines for Sienci's AltMill routers (SLB-EXT, grblHAL),
posting through grblhal.cps - no AltMill post file. Figures from Sienci's
spec pages; the 4x4's travel, rates, homing and spindle range from an
AltMill 4x4's own $$ settings. safe_retract 0.0: the AltMill homes with
machine origin 0 at the homed top, so each tool change lifts G53 G0 Z0,
then T<n> M6 stands alone for gSender/ncSender or the ATC to take over.

Pinned by altmill_machines.rs and the 4x4 two-tool goldens (mm, inch).
Stacked on #715 (grblHAL post).

Fixes #728

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
